class:: FFTFlux2
summary:: Explicit frame-to-frame spectral distance
categories:: UGens>Analysis>MIR
related:: Guides/MIR2, Classes/FFTFlux

description::
Calculates the Euclidean distance between consecutive selected FFT spectra. Positive mode half-wave rectifies bin differences; normalized mode divides by the current frame norm. The first frame and silence return zero.

Previous-frame storage is allocated during construction from code::fftSize::, never when an FFT frame arrives. It is practically similar to link::Classes/FFTFlux:: and link::Classes/FFTFluxPos::, but unifies their behavior behind explicit positive, normalization, spectrum, and frequency options.

classmethods::

method:: kr

argument:: chain
An FFT chain matching code::fftSize::.

argument:: normalize
Nonzero divides distance by the current selected-spectrum norm.

argument:: positive
Nonzero ignores spectral decreases.

argument:: spectrumMode
Literal 0 compares magnitudes and 1 compares powers.

argument:: minFreq
Lowest included frequency in Hz.

argument:: maxFreq
Highest included frequency in Hz; 0 selects Nyquist.

argument:: fftSize
Literal FFT size from 256 through 8192.

returns::
Nonnegative spectral distance.

instancemethods::

examples::
code::
(
Routine({
    var buffer = Buffer.read(s, ExampleFiles.child);
    s.sync;
    {
        var source = PlayBuf.ar(1, buffer, BufRateScale.kr(buffer), loop: 1);
        // For live input instead: source = SoundIn.ar(0);
        var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(1024), source, hop: 0.5);
        FFTFlux2.kr(chain, positive: 1, fftSize: 1024).poll(10, "positive flux");
        (source * 0.15) ! 2
    }.play;
}).play(AppClock);
)
::

